{
  "email": "mei.chen@brightline.example",
  "reason": "Ticket EVAL-email-06: user reports mailbox almost full and some emails failing to send. Checking mailbox.percent_used per KB-010."
}

{
  "outcome": "resolved",
  "reply_to_user": "Hi Mei, thanks for reporting this. Your mailbox is at about 99% of its 50 GB limit, and at 100% Outlook stops sending, which is why some of your emails won't go out. Please free up space with these steps: 1) Empty your Deleted Items and Junk Email folders. 2) Sort your Inbox and Sent Items by size, then delete large emails you no longer need or save their attachments to OneDrive. 3) If you need to keep older mail, let us know and we can turn on Online Archive and move mail older than a year into it. After cleaning up, give it up to an hour for the mailbox to update, then try sending again. If you're still above 95% after cleanup, reply to this ticket and we'll look at whether your role needs a larger quota, which requires manager approval.",
  "internal_note": "lookup_user: mei.chen (user_id 9), active, not blocked, sign-in fine. Mailbox quota 51200 MB, used 50890 MB, percent_used 99.4 (over the 90% warning and at the send-blocking threshold, so send failures are consistent). Followed KB-010 fix steps: user asked to empty Deleted Items/Junk, sort large items by size and offload to OneDrive, and offered Online Archive for old mail. No action tools used. Follow-up: if percent_used is still above 95% after cleanup and the update window (up to 1 hour), escalate per KB-010 for a quota increase that needs manager approval. Device on file: BL-LT-0109 (not checked; not needed for quota issue).",
  "kb_articles": [
    "KB-010"
  ],
  "confidence": "high"
}
